      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-5d48f1880c2b4ea8a6fe25768b777b54" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#ffff80">
        <bounds x="48" y="804" width="185" height="80"/>
        <sourceConnection id="id-02563ed3c1d2404bb14e70a9b13ada5a" source="id-5d48f1880c2b4ea8a6fe25768b777b54" target="id-a3a2f571db7f4c3aa0516ef627893a92"/>
        <content>Centralized Apps Use Case : Apps that access CI data centralized from DiONE client data service</content>
      </child>
      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-1afc6bd4725b4c8cb92cc75c8365ef25" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#ffff80">
        <bounds x="168" y="108" width="185" height="98"/>
        <sourceConnection id="id-8dc0f305d0c84ba5a8e68746c43a3d56" source="id-1afc6bd4725b4c8cb92cc75c8365ef25" target="id-845570304cd24791967a7d87af945b64"/>
        <content>Non centralized app use case : Backends requested by VDI users consuming tokens from the backend server. Backend server is located in the secure zone of its SUCcursale.&#xD;
The proxy is deployed inside the corresponding SUC zone. Multi SUC apps will require to deploy a proxy for each SUC. </content>
      </child>
      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-80340e53385b4661aa15d84811b66443" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#ffff80">
        <bounds x="24" y="348" width="185" height="120"/>
        <sourceConnection id="id-bfe12743115f468ca3347ab8377bec91" source="id-80340e53385b4661aa15d84811b66443" target="id-e503d1724f094efd90eb7352a57cf3d1"/>
        <content>Server to server use case : protected data only, are exchanged between backends, oneway or another.Unprotection occurs with the proxy in the consuming zone applying local visiblity and access rules.</content>
      </child>
