      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-35c9d87e9e794e45b943db7aa10f720c" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#ffff80">
        <bounds x="1128" y="612" width="278" height="246"/>
        <content>Client data visibility rules: &#xD;
- WDX is the master system containing fine grained visibility&#xD;
- RoseGarden assumes the caller has fine grained visibility  on the requested data. The visibility is applied by the calling app OR WDX. &#xD;
- If data is returned by WDX then RoseGarden assumes it can be safely unprotected&#xD;
- RoseGarden will however apply a visibility check of the end user on the requested SUC of the data, regardless the user's physical location.</content>
      </child>
      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-b7b4def8e6ba4d479a7d5e13a246e56d" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#ffff80">
        <bounds x="636" y="816" width="185" height="80"/>
        <sourceConnection id="id-e74277cc054b4dd98b2e0d20f6853fa8" source="id-b7b4def8e6ba4d479a7d5e13a246e56d" target="id-82643af60d8d477893565429b9a86cbf"/>
        <content>It is possible to send tokenized CI data to other apps, even if they are not located in secure / sensitive zone</content>
      </child>
    </element>
